# /etc/exports — what pool-nfs publishes (`exportfs -ra` reads this file).
#
# /pool is the bcachefs pool mount (see init.d/pool-up). The appliance serves
# exactly ONE client across the point-to-point "bench net" /30: the guest is
# 172.31.255.2 (see network/interfaces), the bench client on the host side is
# 172.31.255.1. This /30 is a private lab link, not a LAN — replace the
# client spec with YOUR client before using the image anywhere else:
#
#     192.0.2.10/32(rw,...)     # one client host
#     192.0.2.0/24(rw,...)      # one subnet — think twice with the flags below
#
# Option set (parity with the line the production pool ran):
#   rw                 read-write export;
#   insecure           accept client source ports >1024 (unprivileged clients
#                      bind high);
#   no_subtree_check   suppress subtree filehandle checks — standard for a
#                      volume-wide export, avoids "stale file handle" churn
#                      when files move under a mounted client;
#   no_root_squash     client root maps to server root — required by the bench
#                      protocol (root-owned test trees), safe ONLY on a
#                      point-to-point link. LOUD: never widen the client spec
#                      on a shared network while this flag is set.
/pool 172.31.255.1/30(rw,insecure,no_subtree_check,no_root_squash)
